# .gitignore — BY PATH, NOT BY EXTENSION
#
# Decided 2026-07-29, restated in the charter at §6.4. The reasoning matters more than the
# list: a blanket `*.docx` rule would block the synthetic test fixtures this project needs
# while doing nothing at all about a real client document that had been renamed. So this
# file ignores PLACES, and the pre-commit scan in `tools/` is the actual control.
#
# THIS FILE PREVENTS ACCIDENTS. IT IS NOT A SECURITY CONTROL. It removes nothing already
# committed and does not stop a deliberate `git add -f`. Making a repository public exposes
# the whole history, and a leaked client name cannot be rotated. That is why the material
# below lives OUTSIDE this tree rather than merely being named here.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The three sibling folders that may never enter the repository (charter §6.5).
# They are siblings, so Git cannot see them from here. These entries exist for the
# one case that would defeat that: a copy landing INSIDE the tree, at any depth.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
legal-translation-private/
legal-translation-logs/
legal-translation-test-documents/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE FROZEN INTERMEDIATES — the most content-rich files this project has produced.
# A frozen intermediate is a translated notes file from a real corpus run: it holds the
# document's full source text and its full English text, side by side. The location rule
# has always covered them in principle; naming them by path is the first time it is
# applied to them in practice.
#
# They live in the logs folder, in a per-document working directory. These patterns catch
# that shape wherever it lands, plus the frozen-set directory the harness builds.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tests/frozen/
**/wd/
**/wd-*/
**/lt-logs/
**/orig_unpacked/
**/trans_unpacked/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Scratch, local overrides and build output
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
temp/
*.local

# Packaged skills are BUILD OUTPUT — `tools/package.py` regenerates them at release time.
# What you see in `uk/` and `us/` is what ships; the archive is derived from it.
*.skill

# Renders and conversions produced while checking a document. The rendered visual diff is
# this project's highest-yield instrument and it runs against real client documents.
*.pdf
*.png

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Python
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GENERATED PROBE DOCUMENTS — the builder ships, the output does not
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# tests/probe-5b/make_probe_documents.py builds these from entirely invented text, so they
# are not a confidentiality risk — they are excluded because a GENERATED artefact does not
# need committing when its generator is committed, and because committing them would mean
# widening the "no real document has wandered in" control to a second directory. That
# control allowlists tests/fixtures/ only, and every allowlisted directory is a hole in it.
#
# The distinction from tests/fixtures/, which IS committed: `git bisect` rides on those
# byte-identically, so they have to be stable artefacts. The probe documents have no such
# requirement — regenerate them with one command.
#
# They are written to temp/probe-5b-documents/, so `temp/` above already excludes them from
# git. The path is named here anyway because the CONTROL that matters is not this file: the
# pre-commit gate and the claims check both refuse to see a Word document anywhere outside
# `temp/` and `tests/fixtures/`, and they read the FILESYSTEM rather than the index. A
# gitignored client document is still a client document sitting in the repo (§5.4).
temp/probe-5b-documents/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RUN STATE THAT APPLY DROPS INTO WHATEVER DIRECTORY IT IS POINTED AT. Added 2026-09-02,
# after a real instance reached the index.
#
# `apply_translations_textmatch.py` invokes `validate_translations.py` as its final pre-apply
# pass, and that writes `<workdir>/.validate-state.json` — the batch-cap audit trail — where
# workdir is wherever the NOTES file lives. Hand apply a notes path inside `tests/fixtures/`
# and a state file appears in the committed fixture directory: the working tree goes dirty on
# what the caller thought was a read-only check, `git switch` then refuses, `git bisect`
# breaks, and the next `git add -A` commits run state into a PUBLIC repository.
#
# THIS IS THE GUARD FOR CALLER N+1, NOT THE FIX. The fix is that a test copies its inputs to
# a temp directory before running apply, which `render_diff.py` and `test_stop_deleting.py`
# always did and `test_toc_shapes.py` did not — that caller is corrected in the same commit.
# One line here costs nothing and covers the callers that do not exist yet (§5.1, fix the
# CLASS not the caller). BY PATH, never `*.json`: the fixtures ship their own notes sidecars
# and a blanket rule would silently stop committing them (§2.6, 2026-07-29).
tests/fixtures/.validate-state.json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OS and editor
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
